  "description": "WEGLUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: (C60 H92 Ge12 Ho8 N4 O62)n,2(C12 H8 N2),13(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho7 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5_2 (Ho) has 2 O neighbors; Ho9 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3_2 (Ho) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.724-3.824 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.58-111.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H134Ge12Ho8N8O75. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
